{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^##|''^###'\"' paper_evidence_audit_packet.md; jq '{ok,errors,warnings,hard_errors,compile,latex}' validation_report.json; jq 'keys' references_provenance.json; jq '.final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence | keys' paper_data.json; sed -n '1,80p' build_artifacts.py; sed -n '115,127p' paper.tex\"","aggregated_output":"[\n  \"candidate_diagnostics_trust\",\n  \"episode_count\",\n  \"episodes\",\n  \"path\",\n  \"sha256\",\n  \"status\"\n]\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport statistics\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport matplotlib\nmatplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport numpy as np\nfrom PIL import Image, ImageDraw, ImageFont\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nEPISODE_REF = \"@evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\"\nDECAY_COLORS = {0: \"#28628c\", 1: \"#cb6d32\"}\nOPERATIONS = (\"addition\", \"subtraction\")\n\n\n\ndef sidecar(path, kind, refs=None):\n    payload = {\n        \"schema_name\": \"scientific-evidence.artifact-manifest\",\n        \"artifact\": {\"path\": str(path), \"kind\": kind, \"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()},\n        \"derived_from\": refs or [EPISODE_REF, \"@evidence[[build_artifacts.py]]\"],\n        \"generated_by\": {\"script_path\": \"build_artifacts.py\", \"command\": [\"python\", \"build_artifacts.py\"], \"cwd\": \".\"},\n    }\n    Path(str(path) + \".prov.json\").write_text(json.dumps(payload, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n\n\ndef write_output(path, text, kind):\n    path = Path(path)\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    path.write_text(text)\n    sidecar(path, kind)\n\n\ndef sustained(trace, field, threshold):\n    for index in range(len(trace) - 2):\n        if all(point[field] >= threshold for point in trace[index:index + 3]):\n            return trace[index][\"step\"]\n    return None\n\n\ndef save_plot(figure, stem):\n    figure.savefig(f\"figures/{stem}.pdf\")\n    figure.savefig(f\"figures/{stem}.png\", dpi=300)\n    for suffix in (\"pdf\", \"png\"):\n        sidecar(Path(f\"figures/{stem}.{suffix}\"), \"figure\")\n    plt.close(figure)\n\n\ndef overview_placeholder():\n    target = Path(\"figures/study_overview.png\")\n    log = Path(\"figures/study_overview.prompts.json\")\n    if Path(\".concept_figure_complete\").exists():\n        return\n    if log.exists() and json.loads(log.read_text() or \"{}\"):\n        return\n    if not target.exists():\n        image = Image.new(\"RGB\", (2400, 780), \"white\")\n        drawer = ImageDraw.Draw(image)\n        font = ImageFont.truetype(\"/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSans.ttf\", 48)\n        drawer.rectangle((12, 12, 2388, 768), outline=\"#777777\", width=3)\n        drawer.text((120, 260), \"Study overview reserved for orchestrator rendering\", fill=\"#555555\", font=font)\n        drawer.text((120, 350), \"Not a result plot; see caption for grounded study design\", fill=\"#555555\", font=font)\n        image.save(target, dpi=(300, 300))\n    if not log.exists():\n        log.write_text(\"{}\\n\")\n\n\ndef main():\n    paper_data = json.loads(Path(\"paper_data.json\").read_text())\n    episodes = paper_data[\"final_evaluation\"][\"evaluation_evidence\"][\"episodes\"]\n    widths = tuple(sorted({record[\"case\"][\"width\"] for episode in episodes for record in episode[\"solution\"]}))\n    records = []\n    grouped = defaultdict(list)\n    for episode in episodes:\n        for record in episode[\"solution\"]:\n            case, observed = record[\"case\"], record[\"observations\"]\n            trace = observed[\"trace\"]\nThe input vector is $x=[e_a;e_b]\\in\\mathbb{R}^{194}$, a concatenation of two one-hot encodings. The classifier is\n\\begin{equation}\n f_\\theta(a,b)=W_2\\operatorname{ReLU}(W_1x+b_1)+b_2\\in\\mathbb{R}^{97}.\n\\end{equation}\nThe hidden width $w\\in\\{16,64,256\\}$ gives $292w+97$ trainable parameters: 4,769, 18,785, and 74,849, respectively. Both linear layers have biases. The implementation uses the default PyTorch linear-layer initialization without a width-specific logit-scale calibration. Therefore, the comparison holds the layer family fixed but does not isolate width from all initialization-scale effects.\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L802-L850]]\n\nEach condition minimizes full-batch cross-entropy with AdamW. The fixed learning rate is $\\eta=0.01$ throughout training; weight decay is $\\lambda\\in\\{0,1\\}$, with optimizer coefficients $(0.9,0.999)$ and numerical constant $10^{-8}$. All model parameters are passed to the same optimizer without separate bias exclusions. The recipe controller exposes only a bounded open-loop schedule and receives no training metrics. Its evaluated constant-rate setting is identical across operations, widths, decays, and seeds. The frozen controller and evaluator, rather than proposal descriptions, define the implemented method.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/controller/src/program.py#L46-L78]]\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L842-L870]]\n\nFor constant $\\eta$, the multiplicative shrinkage contribution of AdamW alone is $(1-\\eta\\lambda)^t$ after $t$ updates. This algebra explains why changing a learning-rate recipe would change both gradient updates and accumulated shrinkage. It does not predict the norm or accuracy of the trained network, whose gradient contributions are not removed. We do not compare the fixed recipe empirically against the original lower-rate configuration because no matched final evaluation of that configuration is retained. Nor do we reinterpret development scores as final-task measurements.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
