{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat source_evidence/controller/program_spec.toml; jq '{references: [.references[] | {citation_key,year,authors,title}],safety_boundary}' references_provenance.json; sed -n '169,181p' claims_grounding.json; sed -n '268,279p' paper.tex; sed -n '1,150p' literature/retrieve_approved.py; cat tables/events.tex\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat source_evidence/controller/program_spec.toml; jq '{references: [.references[] | {citation_key,year,authors,title}],safety_boundary}' references_provenance.json; sed -n '169,181p' claims_grounding.json; sed -n '268,279p' paper.tex; sed -n '1,150p' literature/retrieve_approved.py; cat tables/events.tex\"","aggregated_output":"schema_version = 1\ncode_root = \"src\"\n\n[entrypoint]\npath = \"program.py\"\nlanguage = \"python\"\ntype = \"script\"\n\n[copy]\nexclude = [\n  \"**/__pycache__/**\",\n  \"**/*.pyc\",\n  \".venv/**\",\n  \"node_modules/**\",\n  \".git/**\",\n  \".mypy_cache/**\",\n  \".pytest_cache/**\",\n  \".ruff_cache/**\",\n  \".tox/**\",\n  \".nox/**\",\n  \"dist/**\",\n  \"build/**\",\n]\ninclude = [\n]\n\n[integration]\nkind = \"generic\"\nnotes = \"\"\n{\n  \"references\": [\n    {\n      \"citation_key\": \"Power2022GrokkingGB\",\n      \"year\": 2022,\n      \"authors\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Grokking: Generalization Beyond Overfitting on Small Algorithmic Datasets\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"citation_key\": \"Loshchilov2017DecoupledWD\",\n      \"year\": 2017,\n      \"authors\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Decoupled Weight Decay Regularization\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"citation_key\": \"Liu2023Omnigrok\",\n      \"year\": 2022,\n      \"authors\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Omnigrok: Grokking Beyond Algorithmic Data\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"citation_key\": \"Varma2023ExplainingGT\",\n      \"year\": 2023,\n      \"authors\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Explaining grokking through circuit efficiency\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"citation_key\": \"Kumar2024LazyRich\",\n      \"year\": 2023,\n      \"authors\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Grokking as the Transition from Lazy to Rich Training Dynamics\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"citation_key\": \"Davies2023Unifying\",\n      \"year\": 2023,\n      \"authors\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Unifying Grokking and Double Descent\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"citation_key\": \"Nakkiran2020DoubleDescent\",\n      \"year\": 2019,\n      \"authors\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Deep Double Descent: Where Bigger Models and More Data Hurt\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"citation_key\": \"Zhang2017Rethinking\",\n      \"year\": 2016,\n      \"authors\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Understanding deep learning requires rethinking generalization\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"safety_boundary\": \"Only the eight exact identities approved by paper_strategy and the task starter list\"\n}\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"The independent final qualification sources report completed, qualified, and true; this acceptance does not establish generalization or a neural mechanism. The retained diagnostics-trust designation is unverified.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\"final.qualification.status\", \"final.qualification.outcome\", \"final.qualification.correct\", \"final.evidence.episodes\"],\n      \"citation_keys\": [],\n      \"evidence_locator\": \"/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/candidate_diagnostics_trust\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"No matched final-plane comparison to the original lower-rate recipe is retained; development scores are not used as final results, and no cross-task transfer, random-label training, initial-logit calibration, circuit measurement, or generalization-time equivalence is claimed.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"],\n      \"citation_keys\": [],\n      \"source_files\": [\"source_evidence/controller/src/EXPERIMENT_SCOPE.md\", \"source_evidence/controller/src/program.py\", \"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py\"]\n    },\n\\paragraph{Coverage and uncertainty.}\nThe empirical scope is one modulus, one input representation, one hidden-layer family, three widths, two decay values, three initialization seeds, and a fixed split per operation. The operations are closely related, not a representative distribution of algorithmic tasks. The small seed count limits uncertainty assessment; the paired interval pertains only to the implemented capped summary and does not incorporate split variation or hyperparameter selection. We do not pool checkpoint measurements into extra replications, infer confidence from overlapping seed markers, or interpret a zero-width interval as robustness across unseen settings. Reusing a seed aligns the random-number initialization procedure, but differently shaped networks do not have identical initial functions. Likewise, the two operations share an algebraic family while having different fixed input partitions. Pairing improves the definition of a conditional comparison; it does not turn those observations into independent draws from a broad population of models or tasks.\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\n\n\\paragraph{Configuration and evidence boundaries.}\nThe final factorial evaluates one fixed learning-rate recipe. The absence of a matched final result for the original lower-rate configuration precludes a final-baseline improvement claim. The recorded final evaluation completed and was accepted under its specified criteria. That acceptance certifies neither generalization nor a neural mechanism, and the retained metadata does not provide a comprehensive integrity or adaptivity audit. Claims are therefore tied to inspectable evaluator observations and readable implementation snapshots rather than to acceptance labels or hashes alone.\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/grounding_sources/final.qualification.status/value]]\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/grounding_sources/final.qualification.outcome/value]]\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/grounding_sources/final.qualification.correct/value]]\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/candidate_diagnostics_trust]]\n\n\\section{Conclusion}\nimport hashlib\nimport html\nimport json\nimport re\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport requests\n\nAPPROVED = [\n    (\"2201.02177\", \"Power2022GrokkingGB\"),\n    (\"1711.05101\", \"Loshchilov2017DecoupledWD\"),\n    (\"2210.01117\", \"Liu2023Omnigrok\"),\n    (\"2309.02390\", \"Varma2023ExplainingGT\"),\n    (\"2310.06110\", \"Kumar2024LazyRich\"),\n    (\"2303.06173\", \"Davies2023Unifying\"),\n    (\"1912.02292\", \"Nakkiran2020DoubleDescent\"),\n    (\"1611.03530\", \"Zhang2017Rethinking\"),\n]\n\n\ndef clean(text):\n    return html.unescape(re.sub(r\"<[^>]+>\", \"\", text)).strip()\n\n\ndef retrieve():\n    references = []\n    entries = []\n    for identifier, citation_key in APPROVED:\n        url = f\"https://arxiv.org/abs/{identifier}\"\n        response = requests.get(url, timeout=60)\n        response.raise_for_status()\n        document = response.text\n        metadata = {}\n        for name, value in re.findall(r'<meta\\s+name=\"([^\"]+)\"\\s+content=\"([^\"]*)\"', document):\n            metadata.setdefault(name, []).append(html.unescape(value))\n        title = metadata[\"citation_title\"][0]\n        authors = metadata[\"citation_author\"]\n        abstract_match = re.search(r'<blockquote class=\"abstract[^>]*>(.*?)</blockquote>', document, re.S)\n        abstract = clean(abstract_match.group(1)).removeprefix(\"Abstract:\").strip()\n        text = f\"Title: {title}\\nAuthors: {'; '.join(authors)}\\nSource: {url}\\n\\nAbstract consulted:\\n{abstract}\\n\"\n        path = Path(f\"literature/{identifier}.txt\")\n        path.write_text(text)\n        year = metadata[\"citation_date\"][0].split(\"/\")[0].split(\"-\")[0]\n        entries.append(\"@article{\" + citation_key + \",\\n  title={\" + title + \"},\\n  author={\" + \" and \".join(authors) + \"},\\n  year={\" + year + \"},\\n  journal={arXiv preprint arXiv:\" + identifier + \"},\\n  url={\" + url + \"}\\n}\\n\")\n        references.append({\"id\": \"ref.arxiv.\" + identifier, \"citation_key\": citation_key, \"title\": title,\n                           \"source_url\": url, \"year\": int(year), \"retrieved_at\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n                           \"consulted_scope\": \"Title, authors, and abstract only; no citation graph or recommendations read\",\n                           \"local_path\": str(path), \"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()})\n    Path(\"references.bib\").write_text(\"\\n\".join(entries))\n    Path(\"references_provenance.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\"count\": len(references), \"references\": references,\n        \"safety_boundary\": \"Only the eight exact identities approved by paper_strategy and the task starter list\",\n        \"minimum_reference_count_unmet\": True}, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    retrieve()\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\n\\begin{tabular}{llrrrrr}\n\\toprule\nOperation & $\\lambda$ & Width & $T_M^{(1009)}$ & $T_M^{(2027)}$ & $T_M^{(3037)}$ & $G$ observed \\\\\n\\midrule\nAddition & 0 & 16 & 1,500 & 1,000 & 1,000 & 0/3 \\\\\nAddition & 0 & 64 & 500 & 500 & 500 & 0/3 \\\\\nAddition & 0 & 256 & 500 & 500 & 500 & 0/3 \\\\\nAddition & 1 & 16 & \\textemdash & \\textemdash & \\textemdash & 0/3 \\\\\nAddition & 1 & 64 & 500 & 500 & 500 & 0/3 \\\\\nAddition & 1 & 256 & 500 & 500 & 500 & 0/3 \\\\\nSubtraction & 0 & 16 & 1,000 & 1,000 & 1,000 & 0/3 \\\\\nSubtraction & 0 & 64 & 500 & 500 & 500 & 0/3 \\\\\nSubtraction & 0 & 256 & 500 & 500 & 500 & 0/3 \\\\\nSubtraction & 1 & 16 & \\textemdash & \\textemdash & \\textemdash & 0/3 \\\\\nSubtraction & 1 & 64 & 500 & 500 & 500 & 0/3 \\\\\nSubtraction & 1 & 256 & 500 & 500 & 500 & 0/3 \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
